<p>Sudan’s war entered its fourth year on April 15, with fighting between the Sudanese Armed Forces and the Rapid Support Forces still splitting the country and fueling what the United Nations calls the world’s largest humanitarian crisis. Across the coverage, outlets described mass displacement, famine conditions in parts of the country, widespread hunger, and allegations of atrocities, while aid agencies and UN officials warned that global attention has shifted elsewhere even as civilian suffering deepens. A notable development on the anniversary was an international conference in Berlin, where governments and institutions tried to mobilize emergency support for civilians and bring diplomatic attention back to Sudan. Reports said the meeting raised between €1.3 billion and $1.5 billion in pledges, beating the initial goal of about $1 billion and offering some badly needed support, even though a ceasefire still looks distant. Sudan’s government, however, rejected the Berlin conference as interference and objected to the exclusion of the warring parties, underscoring how hard any political breakthrough remains.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/byiCKtGBEhxhkeBU3a6XFIaQEbrU2TXvl7HUog9i5lhuKmY-ZUVi2J2wrR95hXzeBW8UNY4B4PXxNDM_Wtrsl2bHIp9Ey_r_iihawi0AvXpVv6L_eLhbG5h-eZuLemFYjMKp7vN6BI7PTDlOTKrtqE776FLI02NGGDKs1nFyMgMqfdKTiC7HRFhkSSfOqs_6fKBSYpBGqHf-tWpZlD6EkEicDB6Ayywv0879fg7JS2DIDrJU6xu1VpHrKQU2dJ1sUbCNnxalnjlWdkd62Q' alt='Men walk past street vendors&#x27; stands set up beneath a damaged building in Khartoum on April 15.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Frontline shift: The Christian Science Monitor reported that after Sudan was effectively split in two, fighting increasingly centered on the country’s middle belt and the Kordofan/Nuba areas.</li><li>Regional spillover: Berlin donors also discussed support for Sudan’s neighbors affected by the war, a reminder that the conflict reaches beyond Sudan’s borders.</li><li>‘Abandoned crisis’ warning: Officials cited by ABC News and the South China Morning Post said Sudan has become an overlooked emergency as newer wars dominate international attention.</li><li>Arms appeal: UN Secretary-General António Guterres called for weapons flows into Sudan to stop as the war entered its fourth year.</li></ul><blockquote>Sudan remains a test the world is failing - Tom Fletcher</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Sudanese government and pro-army voices: Khartoum said the Berlin meeting ignored Sudan’s sovereignty and denounced what it called a selective, externally imposed process amounting to “colonial tutelage.” (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150678.html'>allAfrica</a>)</li><li>United Nations: UN officials framed the conference as a chance to widen humanitarian access, strengthen relief delivery, and press for a humanitarian truce. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150679.html'>allAfrica</a>)</li><li>German and donor governments: Organizers cast the Berlin gathering less as a venue for direct peace talks and more as an effort to ease civilian suffering and keep Sudan from slipping further off the global agenda. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-hosts-sudan-conference-a-brutal-forgotten-conflict/a-76798246'>DW</a>)</li><li>Sudanese civilians and aid voices: Accounts collected by reporters and aid groups described households cutting meals and navigating daily risks tied to food, safety, and displacement. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/15/2026/sudan-hunger-crisis-deepens-as-the-iran-war-sparks-a-fertilizer-shortage'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/15/nx-s1-5781032/sudan-darfur-war-genocide-famine'>&#x27;Humiliated, broken, powerless&#x27;: Sudan enters fourth year of war</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/explainer-why-is-sudan-at-war-and-what-is-the-impact'>Explainer-Why is Sudan at war, and what is the impact?</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350197/sudan-enters-4th-year-war-abandoned-crisis-grows'>Sudan enters 4th year of war as ‘abandoned crisis’ grows</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150656.html'>Sudan: From Genocide to Countless Acts of Solidarity - Documenting Three Years of War in Sudan</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/15/berlin-conference-seeks-urgent-aid-as-sudan-war-fuels-mass-poverty'>Berlin conference seeks urgent aid as Sudan war fuels mass poverty</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Africa/2026/0415/sudan-civil-war-three-years-kordofan-nuba-mountains'>After 3 years of war, Sudanese civilians pay the price</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/15/2026/sudan-hunger-crisis-deepens-as-the-iran-war-sparks-a-fertilizer-shortage'>Sudan hunger crisis deepens as war enters fourth year</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-canada-aid-sudan-war/'>Canada pledges $120-million in aid for Sudan crisis as war enters its fourth year</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-hosts-sudan-conference-a-brutal-forgotten-conflict/a-76798246'>Berlin hosts Sudan Conference: a brutal, forgotten conflict</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy01d1g0rrjo'>Three years of messages at once - a chronicle of Sudan&#x27;s war pours in as trapped reporter&#x27;s phone turns on</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/apr/15/more-than-1bn-pledged-for-sudan-as-humanitarian-crisis-deepens'>More than £1bn pledged for Sudan as humanitarian crisis deepens</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/sudan-enters-fourth-year-war-officials-lament-abandoned-132051316'>Sudan enters a fourth year of war as officials lament an &#x27;abandoned crisis&#x27;</a> - abcnews.com</